message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "eilikrineia: a public commitment ledger between a person and the AI agents working for them"
abstract: >-
  A single-file, standard-library tool that makes an AI agent's statements to its
  owner accountable. Every statement is committed by salted hash, chained, signed by
  its role key and timestamped on Bitcoin through OpenTimestamps. The chain starts
  with a genesis signed by the owner, who alone can change the key list or the
  auditor's code. Claims are typed: what code can decide (counts, matches, values)
  is decided by code; the rest is read by an auditor model from another vendor,
  which only ever sees short excerpts cut and proven by the program, never whole
  files. A witness in the auditor's separate account detects silent rewriting of
  the unpublished tail within seconds.
